    "text": "96\n\n The Side Letter: Secret Weapon or Legal Landmine?\nHi Sara,\nEver heard someone say, \u201cLet\u2019s just handle that in a side letter,\u201d and thought\u2014that sounds... shady?\nYou\u2019re not alone.\nToday, I\u2019m here to clear the air on side letters\u2014what they are, why they matter, and how one wrong sentence can blow up your whole deal.\nSo, What\u2019s a Side Letter?\nIt\u2019s not a mysterious loophole. A side letter is simply a short agreement that supplements your main contract\u2014like a post-it note stuck to your big purchase agreement. Used well, it\u2019s a tool of precision. Used poorly? It\u2019s chaos.\nHere\u2019s when I see side letters most:\nTo handle last-minute terms without reopening the whole contract\n\nWhen one selling partner wants something unique\u2014like special payment terms or a carveout on a non-compete\n\nTo avoid dragging board members or lenders into review mode over every oddball term\nWhen the parties want to keep some things private, like an individual guarantee or a post-closing referral arrangement\n\nAll of that is totally legit\u2014if you do it right.\nNow Here\u2019s Where It Can All Go Sideways\nThe #1 mistake I see with side letters?\nForgetting about the integration clause in the main agreement.\nThat\u2019s the boring boilerplate at the end that says, \u201cThis is the entire agreement. It overrides anything else we\u2019ve ever said\u2014out loud or in writing.\u201d\nTranslation: if your side letter contradicts the main agreement and doesn\u2019t reference it properly, you could accidentally override the whole thing\u2014or worse, make your side letter completely unenforceable.\nPro tip: Make sure your side letter references the purchase agreement and says it\u2019s intended to supplement, not replace it. If you get that wrong, it could be like swapping the batteries in a smoke alarm\u2026 with raisins. Useless.\nWant to Learn More?\nIf you're deep in the trenches of a deal\u2014or thinking about one\u2014check out our courses at DealAcademy.org or subscribe to our Dealmakers Podcast. I break this stuff down in plain English, so you don\u2019t need a law degree to follow along.\nTo smart, flexible, airtight agreements,\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nBusiness Consultant and Founder of Deal Academy\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers YouTube videos by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
