->\n            \n      <div class=\"mj-column-per-100 mj-outlook-group-fix\" style=\"font-size:0px;text-align:left;direction:ltr;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;width:100%;\">\n        \n      <table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\">\n        <tbody>\n          <tr>\n            <td style=\"vertical-align:top;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;\">\n              \n    <table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"\" width=\"100%\">\n          <tbody>\n            \n                      \n                    <tr>\n                    <td align=\"center\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:10px;padding-right:20px;padding-bottom:10px;padding-left:20px;word-break:break-word;\">\n                      \n      <p style=\"border-top:solid 2px rgba(242, 247, 250, 1);font-size:1px;margin:0px auto;width:100%;\">\n      </p>\n      \n      <!--[if mso | IE]><table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-top:solid 2px rgba(242, 247, 250, 1);font-size:1px;margin:0px auto;width:520px;\" role=\"presentation\" width=\"520px\" ><tr><td style=\"height:0;line-height:0;\"> &nbsp;\n</td></tr></table><![endif]-->\n    \n    \n                    </td>\n                  </tr>\n                    \n                    \n                      \n                    <tr>\n                    <td align=\"left\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:12px;padding-right:24px;padding-bottom:12px;padding-left:24px;word-break:break-word;\">\n                      \n      <div style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.25;text-align:left;color:#000000;\"><h2 style=\"margin-top: 14pt;margin-bottom: 4pt;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The Side Letter: Secret Weapon or Legal Landmine?</span></h2><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Hi Sara,</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Ever heard someone say, \u201cLet\u2019s just handle that in a side letter,\u201d and thought\u2014<em>that sounds... shady</em>?</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">You\u2019re not alone.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Today, I\u2019m here to clear the air on side letters\u2014what they are, why they matter, and how one wrong sentence can blow up your whole deal.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\"><strong>So, What\u2019s a Side Letter?</strong></span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">It\u2019s not a mysterious loophole. A side letter is simply a short agreement that supplements your main contract\u2014like a post-it note stuck to your big purchase agreement. Used well, it\u2019s a tool of precision. Used poorly? It\u2019s chaos.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Here\u2019s when I see side letters most:</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top: 0;margin-bottom: 0;padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li style=\"list-style-type: disc;font-size: 14px;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);background-color: transparent;font-weight: 400;font-style: normal;font-variant: normal;text-decoration: none;vertical-align: baseline;\" dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\"><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">To handle last-minute terms without reopening the whole contract</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type: disc;font-size: 14px;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);background-color: transparent;font-weight: 400;font-style: normal;font-variant: normal;text-decoration: none;vertical-align: baseline;\" dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\"><p style=\"margin-top: 0pt;margin-bottom: 0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">When one selling partner wants something unique\u2014like special payment terms or a carveout on a non-compete</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type: disc;font-size: 14px;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);background-color: transparent;font-weight: 400;font-style: normal;font-variant: normal;text-decoration: none;vertical-align: baseline;\" dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\"><p style=\"margin-top: 0pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">To avoid dragging board members or lenders into review mode over every oddball term<br>When the parties want to keep some things private, like an individual guarantee or a post-closing referral arrangement</span></p></li></ul><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">All of that is totally legit\u2014<em>if</em> you do it right.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\"><strong>Now Here\u2019s Where It Can All Go Sideways</strong></span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">The #1 mistake I see with side letters?</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Forgetting about the integration clause in the main agreement.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">That\u2019s the boring boilerplate at the end that says, \u201cThis is the entire agreement. It overrides anything else we\u2019ve ever said\u2014out loud or in writing.\u201d</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Translation: if your side letter contradicts the main agreement and doesn\u2019t reference it properly, you could accidentally override the whole thing\u2014or worse, make your side letter completely unenforceable.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Pro tip: Make sure your side letter references the purchase agreement and says it\u2019s intended to supplement, not replace it. If you get that wrong, it could be like swapping the batteries in a smoke alarm\u2026 with raisins. Useless.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\"><strong>Want to Learn More?</strong></span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">If you're deep in the trenches of a deal\u2014or thinking about one\u2014check out our courses at</span><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://link.msgsndr.com/email-tracking/57e627846f6?contactId=xoXEjJhxZU4nfwkScSXn\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\"> </span></a><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://link.msgsndr.com/email-tracking/57e627846f6?contactId=xoXEjJhxZU4nfwkScSXn\"><span style=\"color: #3425db !important; color: #3425db !important; font-size: 14px\"><u>DealAcademy.org</u></span></a><span style=\"color: #3425db !important; color: #3425db !important; font-size: 14px\"> </span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">or subscribe to our </span><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://link.msgsndr.com/email-tracking/b17004c1c0b?contactId=xoXEjJhxZU4nfwkScSXn\"><span style=\"color: #3425db !important; color: #3425db !important; font-size: 14px\">Dealmakers Podcast</span></a><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">. I break this stuff down in plain English, so you don\u2019t need a law degree to follow along.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">To smart, flexible, airtight agreements,<br>Sara Sharp<br>Partner, SK&amp;S Law Group<br>Business Consultant and Founder of Deal Academy</span></p></div>\n    \n                    </td>\n                  </tr>\n                    \n                    \n                      \n                    <tr>\n                    <td align=\"left\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:12px;padding-right:24px;padding-bottom:12px;padding-left:24px;word-break:break-word;\">\n                      \n      <div style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.25;text-align:left;color:#000000;\"><p>For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://link.msgsndr.com/email-tracking/e7b72557f90?contactId=xoXEjJhxZU4nfwkScSXn\"><span style=\"color: rgb(52, 37, 219); color: rgb(52, 37, 219)\">Dealmakers Youtube Channel </span></a>where you'll find Sara's <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://link.msgsndr.com/email-tracking/8f022c287b8?contactId=xoXEjJhxZU4nfwkScSXn&amp;v=csIoWCXhXsE&amp;t=15s\" title=\"Weekly Wine Down\"><span style=\"color: rgb(52, 37, 219); font-size: 14px; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif